btain a configuration with exactly \\(k=n-2\\) sunny lines.  \n   - By deleting some of the sunny lines (and adding the corresponding vertical lines) we obtain configurations for every integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n-2\\).\n\n5. **Remaining gap.**  \n   The argument above shows that all integers \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n-2\\) are realizable and that no configuration can have \\(k=n\\). The case \\(k=n-1\\) is still open: the counting argument only rules out \\(k=n\\), while the construction above stops at \\(k=n-2\\). Determining whether \\(k=n-1\\) can occur (or proving it impossible) would complete the classification.\n\n**Conclusion:**  \nI have proved that  \n\\[\n0\\le k\\le n-2\\quad\\text{are all attainable,}\n\\]\nand that any admissible \\(k\\) must satisfy \\(k\\le n-1\\). The status of \\(k=n-1\\) remains unresolved, so a full solution to the problem is not yet obtained.\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
