----------------------------------------------------------\n### Construction for a given \\(k\\)\n\nFix \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n\\) and put  \n\n\\[\np=n-k,\\qquad q=k .\n\\]\n\nThe family  \n\n\\[\n\\mathcal F_k:=\\mathcal L(n-k,k)=\\{x=1,\\dots ,x=n-k\\}\\cup\\{\\,y-x=j-1\\mid 1\\le j\\le k\\,\\}\n\\tag{2}\n\\]\n\nhas exactly \\(n\\) distinct lines:\n\n* the \\(n-k\\) vertical lines are pairwise distinct and non‑sunny;\n* the \\(k\\) lines \\(y-x=j-1\\) have slope \\(1\\), which is different from \\(0\\), \\(\\infty\\) and \\(-1\\); hence they are sunny and also pairwise distinct.\n\nBy the Lemma, \\(\\mathcal F_k\\) covers every point of \\(T_n\\).  \nConsequently \\(\\mathcal F_k\\) satisfies both required conditions and contains precisely \\(k\\) sunny lines.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### Verification of the extremal values\n\n*If \\(k=0\\):* \\(\\mathcal F_0=\\{x=1,\\dots ,x=n\\}\\) – all lines are vertical, none is sunny.\n\n*If \\(k=n\\):* \\(\\mathcal F_n=\\{\\,y-x=j-1\\mid 1\\le j\\le n\\,\\}\\) – all lines have slope \\(1\\), so all \\(n\\) lines are sunny.\n\nBoth cases are specialisations of the general construction above.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### Necessity of the bound\n\nAt most one sunny line can be counted per line, therefore the number of sunny lines cannot exceed the total number of lines, i.e. \\(k\\le n\\).  \nThe construction shows that every integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n\\) is attainable.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### Conclusion\n\nFor the given integer \\(n\\ge 3\\) the set of non‑negative integers \\(k\\) for which there exist \\(n\\) distinct lines satisfying the two stated conditions is exactly  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n\\}} .\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
