nct lines are used, the number of sunny lines cannot exceed \\(n\\); i.e. \\(k\\le n\\).  \nThe construction above shows that every integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n\\) is attainable. Hence no other non‑negative integer can occur.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### Conclusion\n\nFor a given integer \\(n\\ge 3\\) the set of all non‑negative integers \\(k\\) for which there exist \\(n\\) distinct lines satisfying the two stated conditions is precisely  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n\\}} .\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
